{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 32, :comments ["<b>And you shall observe to do all the statutes and the ordinances</b>: Here too he admonishes concerning the statutes and the ordinances before the rest of the commandments. And he will first mention the judgment concerning idolatry and its appurtenances, as I explained in the portion of Va'etchanan (Ramban on Deuteronomy 4:3), and afterward he will mention many ordinances concerning the false prophet and the inciter and the wayward city. And among the statutes he will first mention the offerings in the Sanctuary, and afterward the prohibition against eating any abomination and the rest of the commandments."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {0 "Reading בע\"ז as בְּעֲבוֹדַת זָרָה (concerning idolatry); alternatively it could be read as a heading, 'in [the section beginning with] idolatry,' but the context favors the former."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:14:07.089867110Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}